I find using MMapping makes Gehennom much more fun to play, but I'll 
only use it if I can also cast Detect Treasure and Detect Monsters (in 
that order). Cast all three and it's like you've explored the whole 
level; you can use ';' to see if any of the loot is worth going after, 
and knowing where the monsters are makes it safe enough to avoid them.

It's important to cast the spells in the correct order so the stairs 
aren't hidden by items, and the items aren't hidden by monsters.

